  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Andrew John Bailey (born 30 March 1959) is an English banker who has been Governor of the Bank of England since 16 March 2020. He has also been chair of the Financial Stability Board since 1 July 2025.\nPreviously he served as the Chief Cashier of the Bank of England under Mervyn King from January 2004 until April 2011, Deputy Governor of the Bank of England for Prudential Regulation under Mark Carney from April 2013 to July 2016 and Chief Executive of the Financial Conduct Authority from 2016 to 2020.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
